SUMMARY:Exemption application deadline
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:The statute says before May 1. The chief appraiser may extend o
 nce\, by written order\, for good cause\, by up to 60 days. Basis: Tax Cod
 e §11.43(d)\; §1.06
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Exemption application deadline is in 14 days
TRIGGER:-P14D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Exemption application deadline is in 3 days
TRIGGER:-P3D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dee6f13d-d3b3-53f8-b51f-0a01e7ce74ec@tx-property-tax-protest
DTSTAMP:20270418T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270517
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270518
SUMMARY:Protest filing deadline
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Later of May 15 and 30 days after the notice mailing date. A fi
 rst-class-mail notice is presumed delivered the day it is mailed (rebuttab
 le). A mailed protest is timely if postmarked on or before the last day. I
 f your notice or the CAD shows an earlier date\, protest by the earlier da
 te. Statutory date: Sat\, May 15\, 2027 (Saturday). It moves to the next b
 usiness day\, Mon\, May 17\, 2027. Some county portals close on the origin
 al date\; file by the last business day before it to be safe: Fri\, May 14
 \, 2027. Basis: Tax Code §41.44(a)(1)\; §1.06\; §1.07(c)\; §1.08
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Protest filing deadline is in 14 days
TRIGGER:-P14D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Protest filing deadline is in 3 days
TRIGGER:-P3D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7aa248af-4959-590b-84a7-a46e5e40d1d4@tx-property-tax-protest
DTSTAMP:20270418T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:ARB records-approval date (not an owner deadline)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:The ARB must approve the appraisal records by this date. A prot
 est filed after your deadline can still be heard\, if the ARB finds good c
 ause\, only until the ARB actually approves the records\, which may be ear
 lier. Do not treat this as your filing date. A county of 1\,000\,000 or mo
 re may postpone approval to August 30 by CAD board resolution. Basis: Tax 
 Code §41.44(b)\; §41.12(a)\, (c)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:ARB records-approval date (not an owner deadline) is in 14 days
TRIGGER:-P14D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:ARB records-approval date (not an owner deadline) is in 3 days
TRIGGER:-P3D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e973fdb8-9b1a-5cf4-9506-eca1f9f9bafc@tx-property-tax-protest
DTSTAMP:20270418T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280202
SUMMARY:Taxes become delinquent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Tax is delinquent if not paid before February 1\, so the last d
 ay to pay without penalty is January 31. If the bill is mailed after Janua
 ry 10\, the date is the first day of the next month that gives at least 21
  days after the mailing date. Read the date on your bill. Basis: Tax Code 
 §31.02(a)\; §31.03\; §31.04(a)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Taxes become delinquent is in 14 days
TRIGGER:-P14D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Taxes become delinquent is in 3 days
TRIGGER:-P3D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
